  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "y332-brief",
      "x": 7800,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "Y-332, 6 Sep.\nMaterial 3 Expressive, sage primary, beige for the not-urgent card.\nState is always a mark plus a word.\nDashboard is the entry (the owner picked the rail-and-two-cards direction on 6 Sep); Fleet, Machines and Usage are the tabs; New session opens from the rail; Settings from the avatar.\nOwner, 6 Sep: the search pill stays (it is the D3 command palette, finds and never runs a verb). The Terminal tab's trust banner was cut; trust is answered in the pane or by the Chat tab's option rows, which type the key. Appearance stays."
    },
    {
      "id": "y332-new-session",
      "x": 4680,
      "y": 1200,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "New session, owner's flow of 6 Sep.\n1 name, optional, else a random one; letter and colour tile, or an upload.\n2 machine.\n3 source: GitHub or GitLab repositories, or a local directory. A repository already on the machine opens there; one that is not is cloned under ~/Github or ~/Gitlab.\n4 start: Claude, or a command; other agents later.\n\nNew scope, not in the product yet: cloning from a provider, the GitLab side, the icon and colour on a workspace, and the random name."
    },
    {
      "id": "y332-settings",
      "x": 6240,
      "y": 2400,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "Settings, second draft, 6 Sep.\nOne category at a time, list rows, secrets and long values only in the edit sheet.\nReal today: the ntfy relay per ADR-0021. New scope: hosting and LLM providers as connections, the agent list and its switches, per-event notification switches, SSH identity on the page.\nAppearance added on the owner's ask, reversing Q6's no-theming line: layout (Clean or Compact), colour seed, Light/Dark/System. D3 and Q6 need a dated amendment."
    },
    {
      "id": "y332-form-factors",
      "x": 4800,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "Tablet 834 by 1194 with an M3 navigation rail; phone PWA 390 by 844 with a bottom navigation bar and a FAB for New session. Type sizes hold; rows are 56 px on the phone; order never changes under a finger."
    },
    {
      "id": "y332-chat",
      "x": 4680,
      "y": 4800,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "Chat tab, 6 Sep, drawn to answer \"can the terminal be a chat window\".\nWhat it is: the transcript made writable. Turns come from the agent's JSONL read over ssh (polled, seconds of delay); the composer types into the tmux pane; the trust card's options send the number the agent's own dialog expects.\nNot streaming, and the agent's TUI still lives in the Terminal tab. A streaming chat needs Claude Code's SDK mode instead of the TUI in tmux, which is an ADR-sized change."
    },
    {
      "id": "y333-product-screens",
      "x": 7800,
      "y": 7600,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "Y-333 and Y-334, 6 Sep evening. The routes the product has today, drawn in the new register: one machine (readiness, its workspaces, its tmux sessions; unclaimed ones get Attach and Kill, never Adopt, D6 \u00a74.3), the Spend tab (read on request over ssh; per-model cards carry responses and cost only, because that is what the wire carries; the five counts sit on the total; no fleet total, D6 \u00a75.1), the ended session, Repair (ADR-0020), workspace not found, and the two confirmations. Only Kill and Delete confirm.\n\nAssumed, not ruled: the Kill and Delete dialogs open from a row's overflow menu, which no board draws yet. The Chat tab keeps a Spend tab beside it rather than folding spend into Usage."
    },
    {
      "id": "y334-new-scope",
      "x": 7800,
      "y": 10000,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "New scope in these boards, none of it in the product: Settings General (clone home, default machine, time format), Access (SSH identity, known hosts, the tailnet, which secret backends are found), About's version and update check, the GitHub connect sheet (owner, 6 Sep: Yantra holds the OAuth grant itself, so New session can browse and search private repositories and reviews, issues and pull requests share the sign-in later; git on the machine clones. Where it lives is ADR-0023: the env file beside the relay, never sent to a machine), the remote directory browser and New folder, the four-stage start with a live clone line, and the \u2318K palette (finds a workspace, a machine or a page; never runs a verb)."
    },
    {
      "id": "y335-variants",
      "x": 7800,
      "y": 11200,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "Y-335. Dark is Main recoloured from palette-sage.json's dark roles; tiles keep their colour because they are identity. Weak spots seen: the empty Running track is faint, the Attach pill is near-black on beige. Compact metrics are in BRIEF.md: radius 20, padding 14, rows 40, gaps 8, hero number 44, Idle expanded, a Recent card in the freed space."
    },
    {
      "id": "y336-parity",
      "x": 5760,
      "y": 1320,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "Y-336, tablet. The rail has no top bar, so notifications are a side sheet docked right (420 px), not a popover. Setup dims the rail's destinations and the FAB; bell and avatar stay live."
    },
    {
      "id": "y336-phone",
      "x": 3500,
      "y": 970,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "page-3",
      "text": "Y-336, phone. Settings, notifications, one machine and the confirmations are pushed screens without the bottom bar. The Kill sheet is an M3 bottom sheet. The terminal is the fallback: the pane shows the agent's own dialog and a key row (Esc, Tab, arrows, Ctrl, Enter); Yantra draws no trust buttons of its own."
    }
  ],
